      "case_id": "agent_case_01",
      "answer": "Based on the retrieved results, here are key object detection papers using FPN on COCO between 2018 and 2020:\n\n- **Feature Pyramid Networks for Object Detection** (work_id: `0ccc5f8d-239c-442b-8e43-82a1a6a6597f`): This foundational paper introduces FPN as a generic feature extractor, achieving state-of-the-art results on the COCO detection benchmark when integrated with Faster R-CNN. It specifically evaluates performance using COCO-style Average Precision (AP) and reports results for objects of different sizes.\n\n- **EfficientDet: Scalable and Efficient Object Detection** (work_id: `142db14f-610a-44ca-b928-83aa48f749a0`): This paper proposes a weighted bi-directional feature pyramid network (BiFPN) for improved multi-scale feature fusion. EfficientDet achieves state-of-the-art performance on COCO, with the D7 variant reaching 55.1 AP.\n\n- **Libra R-CNN: Towards Balanced Learning for Object Detection** (work_id: `ee487d82-2719-4276-9ca4-ad54ea102685`): This work introduces a balanced feature pyramid as part of its Libra R-CNN framework, which improves detection performance on COCO by 2.5 points AP compared to the FPN baseline.\n\nWhile the metadata (like year) for these papers is absent in the corpus, the content of these papers confirms their relevance to FPN-based object detection on the COCO dataset.",
