      "answer": "The workspace contains a single paper:\n\n- **Title**: *You Only Look Once: Unified, Real-Time Object Detection*\n- **Authors**: Joseph Redmon, Santosh Divvala, Ross Girshick, Ali Farhadi\n- **Key Contributions**:\n  - YOLO frames object detection as a single regression problem, directly predicting bounding boxes and class probabilities from full images in one evaluation.\n  - The model is extremely fast: the base YOLO processes images at **45 frames per second**, and the smaller Fast YOLO variant runs at **155 frames per second** while still outperforming other real-time detectors in mean Average Precision (mAP).\n  - YOLO generalizes well to new domains. It outperforms methods like R-CNN and DPM when applied to non-natural images such as artwork (tested on Picasso and People-Art datasets), demonstrating robustness beyond its training data.\n\nThese findings are supported by direct quotes from the paper's abstract, experiments, and conclusion sections.",
